BAR", "url": ""}, {"name": "START PAGE WRAPPER", "url": ""}, {"name": "Running Text", "url": ""}, {"name": "Page", "url": ""}, {"name": "BJJ Fighter Database", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/category/bjj-fighters"}, {"name": "Humberto Silveira", "url": ""}, {"name": "BJJ Heroes", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/author/admin"}, {"name": "17.72K", "url": ""}, {"name": "2", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/humberto-silveira-academia-shiozawa"}, {"name": "Breadcrumbs", "url": ""}, {"name": "BJJ Fighter DatabaseCategory", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/category/bjj-fighters"}, {"name": "Category", "url": ""}, {"name": ".breadcrumbs", "url": ""}, {"name": "Humberto Silveira is a Judo and Jiu Jitsu black belt from one of the strongest grappling schools in Bahia (Brazil), the", "url": ""}, {"name": "Academia Schiozawa", "url": ""}, {"name": ", an academy with a very distinct in Brazilian Jiu Jitsu. Humberto is famous for his development of the “", "url": ""}, {"name": "Contato Constante", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-tips-for-fighters/core-muscle-and-mobility-workout"}, {"name": "” (constant contact), a training method that helps the grappling aspect of fighting through a series of movements focused on core strength and hip mobility.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Humberto Silveira Jiu Jitsu", "url": ""}, {"name": "Full Name:", "url": ""}, {"name": "Humberto Silveira Braga", "url": ""}, {"name": "Nickname:", "url": ""}, {"name": "n/a", "url": ""}, {"name": "Kazuo Yoshida", "url": ""}, {"name": "Evaldo Luiz “Serrinha”", "url": ""}, {"name": "Main Achievements:", "url": ""}, {"name": "World Cup Bronze Medallist (2004 – brown)", "url": ""}, {"name": "Favorite Position/Technique:", "url": ""}, {"name": "Weight Division:", "url": ""}, {"name": "Peso Médio", "url": ""}, {"name": "Team/Association:", "url": ""}, {"name": "Academia Shiozawa/ MMA Masters", "url": ""}, {"name": "Humberto Silveira Biography", "url": ""}, {"name": "Humberto Silveira was born in Minas Gerais, Brazil on the 6th of March, 1974. He started practicing Judo when he was 6 years of age, and picked up BJJ years later when he turned 17.", "url": ""}, {"name": "He moved towns as a teenager and joined the Shiozawa gym, led by “Serrinha” a Judo and BJJ black belt. Humberto joined the club to do Judo, but the Jiu Jitsu mindset of the gym started shifting Silveira’s interest towards jiu jitsu and soon he joined the classes on a regular basis.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Though Humberto never appreciated the competition side of both martial arts he practiced, his technique was impeccable, and he progressed through the ranks getting his black belt from Serrinha in 2005 (receiving the second degree in 2008).", "url": ""}, {"name": "In 2005 Humberto spent a 6 months training in Rio de Janeiro with the great master Oswaldo Alves. With the intense training regime he developed a slipped disc and was told by the doctor he would never train again. He lost 70% of his strength on the right side and a sudden loss of muscle mass on his shoulder, arm, pecs and leg. The neurologist condemned Silveira to surgery, but by fate or chance, on that same day Humberto received a Swiss Ball as a present from his mother. Being a physical education buff, Humberto started practicing with the ball regularly which worked as training and physiotherapy. Slowly he started recovering from the loss of mass and strength, and after a while it propelled into the gym and the mats with regular classes being taught with this system. The fantastic results led Humberto to patent the exercises under “Contato Constante” in 2007. He would later travel to the United States by the hand of", "url": ""}, {"name": "Daniel Valverde", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/daniel-valverde"}, {"name": "to further expand the client base.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Academia Shiozawa", "url": ""}, {"name": "Rua da Forca, Piedade", "url": ""}, {"name": "Centro", "url": ""}, {"name": "Salvador-Bahia", "url": ""}, {"name": "Tel. 71 99730019", "url": ""}, {"name": "Tags :", "url": ""}, {"name": "Male Jiu Jitsu Competitors", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/tag/male-bjj-competitors"}, {"name": "Next ArticleContato Constante – Core Muscle/Mobility Training", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-tips-for-fighters/core-muscle-and-mobility-workout"}, {"name": "Next Article", "url": ""}, {"name": "Contato Constante – Core Muscle/Mobility Training", "url": ""}, {"name": "Previous ArticleAugusto Ferrari", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/augusto-ferrari"}, {"name": "Previous Article", "url": ""}, {"name": "Augusto Ferrari", "url": ""}, {"name": "Block Cap", "url": ""}, {"name": "Related Articles", "url": ""}, {"name": "Stream Item", "url": ""}, {"name": "Luiz Dias", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/luiz-dias"}, {"name": "Claudio Mattos “Caloquinha”", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/claudio-mattos-caloquinha-facts-and-bio"}, {"name": "Tayane Porfirio", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/tayane-porfirio"}, {"name": "Michelle Nicolini", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/michelle-nicolini"}, {"name": "Leonardo Silva", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/leonardo-silva"}, {"name": "Laurence Cousin Fouillat", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/laurence-cousin-fouillat"}, {"name": "/.post", "url": ""}, {"name": "Comment", "url": ""}, {"name": "You can start editing here.", "url": ""}, {"name": "2 Comments", "url": ""}, {"name": "Silverback", "url": ""}, {"name": "says:", "url": ""}, {"name": "September 29, 2013 at 4:46 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/humberto-silveira-academia-shiozawa#comment-94199"}, {"name": "Any luck on information about Kazuo Yoshida or a page on Serrinha? Also doesn’t Edson Carvalho come from this linage?", "url": ""}, {"name": "Reply", "url": "#comment-94199"}, {"name": "#comment-##", "url": ""}, {"name": "Donald Travesseiro", "url": ""}, {"name": "Octo