BAR", "url": ""}, {"name": "START PAGE WRAPPER", "url": ""}, {"name": "Running Text", "url": ""}, {"name": "Page", "url": ""}, {"name": "BJJ Fighter Database", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/category/bjj-fighters"}, {"name": "Oswaldo Fadda", "url": ""}, {"name": "BJJ Heroes", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/author/admin"}, {"name": "161.83K", "url": ""}, {"name": "42", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio"}, {"name": "Breadcrumbs", "url": ""}, {"name": "BJJ Fighter DatabaseCategory", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/category/bjj-fighters"}, {"name": "Category", "url": ""}, {"name": ".breadcrumbs", "url": ""}, {"name": "Oswaldo Fadda was an important figure in the development of", "url": ""}, {"name": "in Brazil, being also the main alternative of the Brazilian grappling style to", "url": ""}, {"name": "Gracie family", "url": "/?tag=gracie-family"}, {"name": ", and one of the few men that achieved the rank of", "url": ""}, {"name": "red belt", "url": "/?tag=bjj-red-belts"}, {"name": "(9th degree/", "url": ""}, {"name": "nono grau", "url": ""}, {"name": "). Oswaldo Fadda became an influential figure for the growth of jiu jitsu working from the outskirts of Rio de Janeiro, where he set his own academy in the 1950’s. In recent times, the main academies developed under the Oswaldo Fadda are", "url": ""}, {"name": "Nova Uniao", "url": "/?p=2198"}, {"name": "and", "url": ""}, {"name": "GFTeam", "url": "/?p=1579"}, {"name": "Oswaldo Fadda Jiu Jitsu", "url": ""}, {"name": "Full Name:", "url": ""}, {"name": "Oswaldo Baptista Fadda", "url": ""}, {"name": "Nickname:", "url": ""}, {"name": "N/A", "url": ""}, {"name": "Mitsuyo Maeda", "url": ""}, {"name": "Luis França", "url": "/?p=2443"}, {"name": "Main Achievements:", "url": ""}, {"name": "Favourite Technique:", "url": ""}, {"name": "His school was famous for using footlocks", "url": ""}, {"name": "Weight Division:", "url": ""}, {"name": "Association/Team:", "url": ""}, {"name": "Academia FADDA", "url": ""}, {"name": "Oswaldo Fadda Biography", "url": ""}, {"name": "Oswaldo Fadda was born in Bento Ribeiro – State of Rio de Janeiro on the 15th of January 1921. Fadda started training in 1937 after he joined the Brazilian Marines. His coach was", "url": ""}, {"name": ", a former student of Mitsuyo Maeda who achieved his grade of instructor (allegedly*) around the same time as", "url": ""}, {"name": "Carlos Gracie", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/carlos-gracie-sr-profile"}, {"name": ", the founder of the", "url": ""}, {"name": "Gracie Jiu Jitsu Academy", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/featured/gracie-humaita-academy"}, {"name": "Oswaldo Fadda received his instructor grade from the hands of his coach (França) in 1942 and soon after began teaching the style himself, from his home town in the outskirts of Rio de Janeiro.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Always trying to promote jiu jitsu as a way of life, with a strong sense of discipline and honor, Master Oswaldo Fadda would often perform demonstrations on public squares, beaches,", "url": ""}, {"name": "favelas", "url": ""}, {"name": "(slums), outside churches and even in circuses and church patios. On the 27th of January 1950 Oswaldo Fadda finally opened his very own academy fully dedicated to martial arts.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Throughout his coaching career, Fadda was often portrayed as an outcast by jiu jitsu practitioners in the “", "url": ""}, {"name": "Zona Sul", "url": ""}, {"name": "” and town centre of Rio de Janeiro, who failed to see the potential of an academy in the suburbs. This ‘lack of respect’ caused Fadda to issue a challenge to the Gracie Academy in 1951, the contest was proposed through the media, in the", "url": ""}, {"name": "Globo Jornal", "url": ""}, {"name": "and it went as follows:", "url": ""}, {"name": "We wish to challenge the Gracies, we respect them like the formidable adversaries they are but we do not fear them. We have 20 pupils ready for the dispute.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Helio Gracie", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/?p=44"}, {"name": "accepted the challenge and the competition was booked for the Gracie Academy. Oswaldo Fadda’s team won, making better use of their footlock knowledge, something Helio frowned upon, calling it “suburban technique” (t", "url": ""}, {"name": "écnica de suburbano", "url": ""}, {"name": ") – according to Reila Gracie’s biography of Carlos Gracie. The highlight of the competition was when Fadda’s pupil, José Guimarães, choked Gracie representative Leonidas to sleep.", "url": ""}, {"name": "The event had good media coverage, which had a double effect. While the victories gave Oswaldo’s team notoriety (and more students) it also brought the interest of all the hard men of the nearby towns, who would often stop by Fadda’s academy to issue challenges to Master Oswaldo and his students. These challenges gained such proportions that Master Fadda decided to start taking one day off from the weekly schedule, where he closed the doors of the academy to fight any challengers. It is said that jiu jitsu never lost a fight.", "url": ""}, {"name": "In 1967 the first jiu jitsu federation is born, named “Federação de Jiu-Jitsu da Guanabara” in Rio de Janeiro. This organization was created with the approval of the national Secretaries of State. The rules were very basic and differed tremendously from today’s tournaments. According to research done by", "url": ""}, {"name": "GracieMag", "url": "http://www.graciemag.com/pt/historia-do-jiu-jitsu/"}, {"name": "back in 2014, positions such as takedowns and mount and back takes accounted for 1 point, and matches would last 5 minutes with 3 of overtime (adults). Helio Gracie became the president of the federation, while the illustrious Fadda took a position in the office as vice president of the technical cabinet (president being Carlson Gracie).", "url": ""}, {"name": "Oswaldo Fadda spent the rest of his days in his hometown of Bento Ribeiro, like the humble man he was, with his students and his family. With age he started suffering from Alzheimer’s disease. Struggling with the illness for years, he finally succumbed to bacterial pneumonia in April 2005, at 84 years of age.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Tags :", "url": ""}, {"name": "1950s Jiu Jitsu", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/tag/1950s-bjj"}, {"name": "1960s Jiu Jitsu", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/tag/1960s-bjj"}, {"name": "BJJ Red Belts", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/tag/bjj-red-belts"}, {"name": "Male Jiu Jitsu Competitors", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/tag/male-bjj-competitors"}, {"name": "Next ArticleGeorge Gracie", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/george-gracie-facts-and-bio"}, {"name": "Next Article", "url": ""}, {"name": "George Gracie", "url": ""}, {"name": "Previous ArticleOsvaldo Alves", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/osvaldo-alves-facts-and-bio"}, {"name": "Previous Article", "url": ""}, {"name": "Osvaldo Alves", "url": ""}, {"name": "Block Cap", "url": ""}, {"name": "Related Articles", "url": ""}, {"name": "Stream Item", "url": ""}, {"name": "Rerisson Gabriel", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/rerisson-gabriel"}, {"name": "Kim Terra", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/kim-terra"}, {"name": "Nathalie Ribeiro", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/nathalie-ribeiro"}, {"name": "Giovanna Carneiro", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/giovanna-carneiro"}, {"name": "Gabriel Figueiró", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/gabriel-figueiro"}, {"name": "Emilio Hernandez", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/emilio-hernandez"}, {"name": "/.post", "url": ""}, {"name": "Comment", "url": ""}, {"name": "You can start editing here.", "url": ""}, {"name": "42 Comments", "url": ""}, {"name": "Ade", "url": ""}, {"name": "says:", "url": ""}, {"name": "April 2, 2011 at 5:18 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-4596"}, {"name": "great man, did not have the same popullarity as the gracies but was as good as them.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Reply", "url": "#comment-4596"}, {"name": "fullonbj", "url": ""}, {"name": "February 12, 2018 at 10:38 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-314249"}, {"name": "Just curious, did Fadda fight in vale tudo fights? How about Luis França Filho? We understand that they are a non-Gracie , but what is their contribution to vale tudo?", "url": ""}, {"name": "Was their contribution more towards sport BJJ or more towards jiujitsu as a form of combat?", "url": ""}, {"name": "#comment-##", "url": ""}, {"name": ".children", "url": ""}, {"name": "manny", "url": "http://www.jiujitsusweep.com"}, {"name": "May 5, 2011 at 12:45 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-4879"}, {"name": "wow i never knew there were others besides the Gracies to learn jiu jitsu from Maeda. So cool, we need more articles like this !!", "url": ""}, {"name": "Jason", "url": ""}, {"name": "August 10, 2012 at 4:06 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-19111"}, {"name": "Maeda had a lot of students throughout Latin America. Long before he arrived in Brazil he lived in Mexico, Cuba, and throughout central America. He helped introduce judo (Kano jiu-jitsu) to those countries.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Unfortunately, his teachings didn’t spread or last in many of those countries like it did in Brazil. He left Mexico in 1910, which was the year the Mexican Revolution (1910-1920) started, which could be a/the reason why jiu-jitsu didn’t spread.", "url": ""}, {"name": "In Cuba he had more success, which is probably why Cubans are some of the best judokas around. Maeda along with three other Japanese judo masters were known as the “Four Kings of Cuba”. From Cuba he finally went to Brazil.", "url": ""}, {"name": "DGonza70", "url": ""}, {"name": "January 16, 2013 at 5:41 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-22006"}, {"name": "Great info!!! Thanks for the insight!!!!", "url": ""}, {"name": "James Soetebeer", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/people/James-Soetebeer/1826906389"}, {"name": "June 14, 2011 at 9:06 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-5156"}, {"name": "Rodolfo Viera, who just choked out Rubens " Cobrinha "  Charles in Abu Dhabi, is of non-Gracie BJJ . I am a Gracie Jiujitsu black belt and I never new about the Luis Franca until recently. Also, check out Luta Livre for a unique, no-gi grappling from Brazil that developed completely apart from jiujitsu.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Arctic Alliance", "url": ""}, {"name": "January 23, 2012 at 12:22 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-8711"}, {"name": "I'm with the Alliance Team and I was bummed to see that, but Cobrinha is a almost unbeatable at his chosen weight class, Vieira is a beast though, that judo enhanced top game of his is super dangerous.", "url": ""}, {"name": "I was suprised to see the existance of another as well. Funny that Fadda's school is the reason why they frown on footlocks hahaha.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Brian Mendez", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/brian.mendez.716"}, {"name": "February 21, 2014 at 10:14 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-97858"}, {"name": "Fadda to the Gracie's is like Mary Magdalene and Jesus to the Catholic Church, they knew about it but didn't let anyone else know about it and keep it on the under ground", "url": ""}, {"name": "Francisco Rodriguez", "url": ""}, {"name": "November 26, 2024 at 4:39 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-488992"}, {"name": "What??? Reading too much Davinci Code…lol!", "url": ""}, {"name": "John", "url": ""}, {"name": "July 19, 2011 at 3:27 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-5402"}, {"name": "This was an eye opening article for me as well.  I thought only Gracies could receive a red belt.", "url": ""}, {"name": "bjjheroes", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com"}, {"name": "July 19, 2011 at 4:31 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-5405"}, {"name": "Hi John, not at all! There have been many other red belts (Pedro Hemeterio, Osvaldo Alves, Armando Wridt, etc, etc). The 5 original Gracies are the only ones that had the rank of 10th degree. That degree is applicable only to the founding fathers of the style", "url": ""}, {"name": "Adrian Luna", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/DudeitsmeAdrian"}, {"name": "August 27, 2011 at 10:14 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-5754"}, {"name": "Does anyone find it a little wrong that there is not much information on Luis França Filho? He doesn't even have a page in BJJ Heroes. I just recently found out that Brazilian Jiu Jitsu didn't come from just the Gracies. This might just be the BJJ nerd in me, but I feel a litle lied to. Throughout my 5 years being involved with Jiu Jitsu and MMA all I've heard from the Gracies is how they brought Jiu Jitsu to the world. If possible I'd love to learn more about this remarkable man (Professor Fadda), Luis França Filho, and Non- Gracie BJJ in general. Hey BJJ  Heroes! Maybe you should sponsor a trip to Brazil for me so I can get more information out to you and the world, maybe a documentary?  😉", "url": ""}, {"name": "August 28, 2011 at 3:06 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-5755"}, {"name": "Hey Adrian, it is hard to find information on Luis França. Jiu Jitsu wasn't big in those days, and there is not alot of info around about the non Gracie , though there were a few guys outside the Gracies teaching similair styles. As for your campaign for a trip to Br, if I had the money I would go myself 😛", "url": ""}, {"name": "Andre Cury", "url": ""}, {"name": "June 3, 2018 at 7:45 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-319853"}, {"name": "Master Edmilson Alvez is a living legend from that .. very humble man, if you have any questions look for him.", "url": ""}, {"name": "August 28, 2011 at 9:30 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-5763"}, {"name": "Haha figured it was worth a try :p", "url": ""}, {"name": "Coach RP", "url": "http://www.evolvemma.com.au"}, {"name": "August 30, 2011 at 7:19 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-5814"}, {"name": "EvolveMMA.com.au has a 2nd degree black belt under Master Wilson and under Professor Fadda its Professor Minol, his our full time coach and he leads the Evolve Team. EvolveMMA is Minols headquarters as the head coach with 2 of his black belts and 3 blue belts.", "url": ""}, {"name": "come down and see us", "url": ""}, {"name": "http://www.evolvemma.com.au", "url": "http://www.evolvemma.com.au"}, {"name": "Sharneet", "url": ""}, {"name": "June 30, 2013 at 8:55 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-90362"}, {"name": "Professor Minol Tavares Tutida is no longer teaching at Evolve MMA. he has opened his own club in Preston Victoria Australia. Come down and learn the FADDA of Brazilian Jiujitsu.", "url": ""}, {"name": "fadda line", "url": ""}, {"name": "December 17, 2016 at 11:20 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-300882"}, {"name": "minol originally was black belt under carlos toyota in japan whos under osvaldo alves", "url": ""}, {"name": "December 17, 2016 at 11:44 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-300883"}, {"name": "he got his bb from eduardo da rocha not carlos toyota. my mistake. so hes a true faddal from white to black", "url": ""}, {"name": "Marcelo", "url": ""}, {"name": "October 28, 2019 at 3:01 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-349571"}, {"name": "Robert Drysdale is doing a major documentary on the REAL history of BJJ and everyone is excited! The Gracies will hate him but people deserve to know the Fadda", "url": ""}, {"name": "Ramses", "url": ""}, {"name": "October 14, 2011 at 10:32 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-7334"}, {"name": "Are there any videos out there that teaches you the basics? something like what the Gracie have", "url": ""}, {"name": "Jorge", "url": ""}, {"name": "November 13, 2011 at 12:25 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-7756"}, {"name": "Any info on Master Deo? Or Ronny Lis? Would really appreciate it,great job with the site.", "url": ""}, {"name": "esjenk", "url": ""}, {"name": "December 3, 2011 at 9:41 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-7995"}, {"name": "Great article. It's Great to read about the other branch of BJJ and this Mr. Fadda.    I'm NOT a Gracie hater at all, but I have to always kinda laugh when I hear someone say that," It all came from the Gracies."  or  "The Gracies invented ju-jitsu."   When I ask them what language does the word ju-jitsu come from ? Or show them a 1950s Judo textbook showing a armbar, it hilarious and watch them still try to fumble and stumble with a reply. The fact is,yes the Gracies took an existing art and refined,modified and added to it but they didn't invent ju-jitsu,the armbar or gi/no gi grappling. There are many forms of grappling that pre-date the Gracies that have similar or the same armbars,leglocks,chokes and takedowns.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Paul", "url": ""}, {"name": "December 7, 2013 at 5:11 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-96350"}, {"name": "You won't believe how hard it is to find someone like you.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Michael", "url": ""}, {"name": "January 14, 2012 at 7:18 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-8525"}, {"name": "In fairness, the Gracies were the ones who exposed the world to their version of jujitsu/judo. Could Oswaldo's have done the same? Yes, but it didn't.", "url": ""}, {"name": "edgar", "url": ""}, {"name": "January 15, 2012 at 8:32 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-8546"}, {"name": "yes, they did. its alive here in TX", "url": ""}, {"name": "Todd", "url": ""}, {"name": "January 19, 2012 at 11:04 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-8638"}, {"name": "AFTER the Gracies had already brought BJJ out of Brazil and into the world. After the Gracies opened the door, everybody and their mothers started coming to the U.S. to rip the benefits.  If it was for the Fadda , maybe we would still not know what BJJ was till this day.", "url": ""}, {"name": "islandfrere", "url": ""}, {"name": "April 8, 2012 at 9:24 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-10616"}, {"name": "if fadda had 20 children then yes Fadda Jiu Jitsu would be just as big.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Leo P O'Brien", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/leo.obrien"}, {"name": "April 15, 2012 at 9:00 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-10915"}, {"name": "lol…Yes the Gracies are certainly fertile…..", "url": ""}, {"name": "Kail", "url": ""}, {"name": "September 17, 2024 at 12:31 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-482619"}, {"name": "The 21 children played a significant role in spreading Brazilian jiu jitsu, but the financial support and media exposure were also crucial. The Gracies marketed a narrative that they were the sole creators of Brazilian jiu jitsu, overshadowing the contributions of many others involved in its development. The Gracies, who were from an upper-class background, aimed to dominate BJJ and control its financial aspects. Oswaldo Baptista Fadda was a notable practitioner and innovator of Brazilian jiu-jitsu, achieving the rank of ‘nono grau’ (9th degree red belt). In 2014, he was posthumously honored with the 10th degree (‘décimo grau’). Fadda is recognized as one of the highest-ranked non-Gracie black belts and for his efforts in teaching students from the poorer regions of Rio de Janeiro, where Brazilian jiu-jitsu was traditionally seen as an upper-class sport. His , the most prominent after the Carlos Gracie , continues today through teams like Nova União, Grappling Fight Team, Deo Jiu-Jitsu (Deoclecio Paulo), and Equipe Mestre Wilson Jiu-Jitsu (Wilson Pereira Mattos). Even without substantial financial backing and media coverage, Fadda’s team managed to defeat the Gracies. The Gracies are not superior in Brazilian jiu jitsu; they simply have better funding and connections.", "url": ""}, {"name": "I would love to see a documentary that reveals the true history of Brazilian jiu jitsu and highlights that the Gracies did not want the less privileged to participate in the sport.", "url": ""}, {"name": "January 15, 2012 at 8:36 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-8547"}, {"name": "do some research on Deo Jiu Jitsu. a red belt from a non gracie linage. FADDA JIU JITSU", "url": ""}, {"name": "BJJcali", "url": ""}, {"name": "June 5, 2012 at 11:47 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-12802"}, {"name": "Wow one could argue that this great man was even greater than helio in wanting to spread bjj to all people which is where the falling out happened cause helio wanted to keep it in the richer areas", "url": ""}, {"name": "guambjj", "url": ""}, {"name": "June 30, 2012 at 5:55 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-17717"}, {"name": "If you guys didnt already know 1 of the 2 guys whos started nova uniao is from the same . His name is alexander wall abd he teamed up with andre pedeneirasto create one of the most prestigous schools out there ! Another sick that i was very interested to come across was reyson gracie and oswaldo alves who if in not mistaken is jacare souza and andre galvaos !", "url": ""}, {"name": "July 1, 2012 at 4:52 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-18036"}, {"name": "Hey Guam. The co founder of Nova União, Wendel Alexander is also on BJJ Heroes.", "url": ""}, {"name": "July 5, 2012 at 12:11 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-18597"}, {"name": "lol ! im sorry ima lil rusty about his name ! i read about nova uniao a while ago !", "url": ""}, {"name": "Andrew Dearsley", "url": ""}, {"name": "January 17, 2013 at 2:26 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-22024"}, {"name": "I recieved my Brown belt of a direct student of Grand master Fadda in 2005. " Master Edson Leonardo Da Silva  was just promoted to 7th degree "carol" red and black belt by Grand master Fadda in Japan just before his death. His has a large influence for BJJ in Japan. I always enjoy tell people why heel hooks and other leg submissions were banned in BJJ completion.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Jason Kay", "url": ""}, {"name": "June 12, 2013 at 4:50 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-85612"}, {"name": "Why are heel hooks banned for bjj competitions Andrew?Is it because of Fadda's students using it with so much success against Hellio's students?  I thought all other leg locks are legal(at least from brown and above) and heel hooks are legal in professional grappling tournaments, like the NAGA elite division and ADCC. Anyway i personally think it's a positive think that heel hooks are banned!", "url": ""}, {"name": "edgardo venegas", "url": ""}, {"name": "March 12, 2013 at 9:12 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-27601"}, {"name": "Franca, Fadda, Deo and Lis Jiu-Jitsu linage lives in the US, here in Laredo, Texas and Austin with Professor Ronny Lis.", "url": ""}, {"name": "January 9, 2014 at 10:47 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-96824"}, {"name": "Grappling Fight Team! ( GFT ) Some of the worlds most prominent BJJ black belts in the world. Luis Franca – Oswaldo Fadda –  Monir Salomão – Julio Cesar Pereira", "url": ""}, {"name": "darryl mcmillan", "url": ""}, {"name": "January 16, 2014 at 5:03 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-97064"}, {"name": "Hi my name is darryl mcmillan, im married to master carley gracie daughter heather gracie of largo fl.we argue the fact that her family wasn't the 1st to start bjj, shes so bullhead, she wont read the history", "url": ""}, {"name": "George", "url": ""}, {"name": "March 7, 2016 at 8:21 pm", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-297493"}, {"name": "Any info on the Gommes would be appreciated.thanks", "url": ""}, {"name": "Ariel A Fernandez", "url": ""}, {"name": "August 26, 2020 at 5:47 am", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#comment-366450"}, {"name": "Can someone identify all of the people in the image at the header of the page. I have taken a real interest in the history and of Oswaldo Fadda. Thanks!", "url": ""}, {"name": "Leave A Reply", "url": ""}, {"name": "Cancel Reply", "url": "/bjj-fighters/oswaldo-fadda-facts-and-bio#respond"}, {"name": "Your email address will not be published.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Save m