BAR", "url": ""}, {"name": "START PAGE WRAPPER", "url": ""}, {"name": "Running Text", "url": ""}, {"name": "Page", "url": ""}, {"name": "BJJ Fighter Database", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/category/bjj-fighters"}, {"name": "Rodnei Barbosa", "url": ""}, {"name": "BJJ Heroes", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/author/admin"}, {"name": "26.74K", "url": ""}, {"name": "0", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-fighters/rodnei-barbosa"}, {"name": "Breadcrumbs", "url": ""}, {"name": "BJJ Fighter DatabaseCategory", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/category/bjj-fighters"}, {"name": "Category", "url": ""}, {"name": ".breadcrumbs", "url": ""}, {"name": "Rodnei Barbosa, commonly known as “Roy”, is a", "url": ""}, {"name": "Brazilian jiu-jitsu", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/bjj-news/brazilian-jiu-jitsu"}, {"name": "black belt under the prestigious", "url": ""}, {"name": "Paulo Rezende", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/?p=6006"}, {"name": ", a coach known for having developed grapplers such as", "url": ""}, {"name": "Marcelo Garcia", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/?p=16"}, {"name": "Reinaldo Ribeiro", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/?p=1149"}, {"name": "Rodrigo Ranieri", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/?p=1440"}, {"name": "Matheus Diniz", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/?p=5423"}, {"name": ", and many others. Coming from one of the most successful s in the sport, Barbosa earned his place in the sport with wins at the World (no-gi), South American and Brazilian National Championships as well as New York, Rio and London International Opens.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Rodnei Barbosa Jiu-Jitsu", "url": ""}, {"name": "Full Name:", "url": ""}, {"name": "Rodnei Barbosa Gabriel Junior", "url": ""}, {"name": "Nickname:", "url": ""}, {"name": "“Roy” which is short for Rodnei. Barbosa trained at a Paulo Rezende affiliate gym up until 2013 when he moved to Rezende’s main academy. Coach Paulo had difficulty pronouncing Rodnei, so he started calling him Roy.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Carlos Gracie", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/?p=36"}, {"name": "Helio Gracie", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/?p=44"}, {"name": "Carlson Gracie", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/?p=22"}, {"name": "Fernando “Pinduka”", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/?p=690"}, {"name": "Leonardo Castello Branco", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/?p=935"}, {"name": "Main Achievements:", "url": ""}, {"name": "1st Place UAEJJF Abu Dhabi Pro (2017)", "url": ""}, {"name": "1st Place IBJJF European Open (2019)", "url": ""}, {"name": "1st Place CBJJ Brazilian Nationals (2017/2016)", "url": ""}, {"name": "1st Place IBJJF South American Championship (2017)", "url": ""}, {"name": "2nd Place IBJJF World Championship (2018 / 2019)", "url": ""}, {"name": "2nd Place IBJJF World Championship NOGI (2019)", "url": ""}, {"name": "2nd Place IBJJF Pan Championship (2024)", "url": ""}, {"name": "2nd Place IBJJF European Championship NOGI (2019)", "url": ""}, {"name": "2nd Place CBJJ Brazilian Nationals (2019)", "url": ""}, {"name": "2nd Place IBJJF European Open (2016)", "url": ""}, {"name": "2nd Place IBJJF American Nationals (2023)", "url": ""}, {"name": "3rd Place IBJJF World Championship (2021 / 2024)", "url": ""}, {"name": "3rd Place IBJJF World Championship NOGI (2023)", "url": ""}, {"name": "Main Achievements (Coloured Belts):", "url": ""}, {"name": "1st Place CBJJ Brazilian Nationals (2015 brown, 2014 purple)", "url": ""}, {"name": "1st Place IBJJF World No-Gi Championship (2015 brown)", "url": ""}, {"name": "1st Place IBJJF South American Championship (2014 brown)", "url": ""}, {"name": "1st Place IBJJF Rio International Open (2014 brown)", "url": ""}, {"name": "1st Place IBJJF London Winter International Open(2015 brown)", "url": ""}, {"name": "1st Place IBJJF New York Summer International Open (2015 brown)", "url": ""}, {"name": "2nd Place IBJJF European Open (2015 brown)", "url": ""}, {"name": "2nd Place CBJJ Brazilian Nationals (2014 purple)", "url": ""}, {"name": "2nd Place IBJJF Rio Fall International Open (2015 brown)", "url": ""}, {"name": "3rd Place IBJJF European Open (2016)", "url": ""}, {"name": "Favorite Position/Technique:", "url": ""}, {"name": "Deep", "url": ""}, {"name": "Half Guard", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/techniques/half-guard"}, {"name": "Weight Division:", "url": ""}, {"name": "Peso Galo (57kg/125lbs)", "url": ""}, {"name": "Team/Association:", "url": ""}, {"name": "Zenith BJJ", "url": ""}, {"name": "Rodnei Barbosa Biography", "url": ""}, {"name": "Rodnei Barbosa was born on January 14, 1995, in Formiga – Minas Gerais, Brazil. The same town where well-known grapplers such as", "url": ""}, {"name": "came from.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Martial arts appeared in Rodnei’s life at the age of 6, through capoeira, a style he practiced for 1 year. Due to Barbosa’s parents’ dire economic situation, he had to leave his capoeira days on standby. He returned to martial arts when he was 9 years old, through a social project led by Lourenço Nascimento at the town’s university where he first learned about jiu-jitsu.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Under Lourenço Nascimento’s guidance, Rodnei went through the belt system up until 2013 when Rodnei decided to make of jiu-jitsu his career, choosing to move away from Formiga and joining", "url": ""}, {"name": "‘s headquarters academy in Poço de Caldas – MG, a gym to which Lourenço Nascimento was affiliated to. At Rezende’s gym, Rodnei joined Rezende’s famous fighter house. A place where coach “Paulao” shelters the team’s pro-athletes, providing them a roof, food and training. A place that has produced several talented athletes such as the aforementioned Reinaldo Ribeiro, Marcelo Garcia, Matheus Diniz and many more.", "url": ""}, {"name": "On the 24th of November, 2015. Rodney Barbosa was awarded his black belt from the hands of the prestigious coach Paulo Rezende, becoming Paulao’s 234th black belt.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Rodnei Barbosa Grappling Record", "url": ""}, {"name": "79 WI