nal Champion (2017)", "url": ""}, {"name": "IBJJF Los Angeles Open Champion (2018)", "url": ""}, {"name": "CBJJ Brazilian National Teams Championship 2nd Place (2016)", "url": ""}, {"name": "IBJJF Pan Championship 3rd Place (2018)", "url": ""}, {"name": "Main Achievement (Colored Belts):", "url": ""}, {"name": "CBJJ Brazilian National Champion (2015 brown)", "url": ""}, {"name": "CBJJ Brazilian National No-Gi Champion (2015 brown)", "url": ""}, {"name": "IBJJF South American Champion (2015 brown)", "url": ""}, {"name": "IBJJF Rio BJJ Pro Champion (2015 brown)", "url": ""}, {"name": "IBJJF Rio Fall International Open Champion (2015 brown)", "url": ""}, {"name": "IBJJF Rio Winter International Open Champion (2015 brown)", "url": ""}, {"name": "IBJJF European Open 3rd Place (2016 brown)", "url": ""}, {"name": "Favorite Position/Technique:", "url": ""}, {"name": "Good overall game", "url": ""}, {"name": "Weight Division:", "url": ""}, {"name": "Peso Leve (76kg/168lbs)", "url": ""}, {"name": "Team/Association:", "url": ""}, {"name": "Ares BJJ", "url": ""}, {"name": "Breno Bittencourt Biography", "url": ""}, {"name": "Breno Bittencourt was born on July 7, 1989 in Rio de Janeiro – Brazil.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Having in his father a big no-holds-barred fan with combat experience, it didn’t take long for young Breno to have his first steps in martial arts, steps that took place at the age of 4 in judo class.", "url": ""}, {"name": "As a 13 year old Breno Bittencourt added jiu jitsu to his off-school activities, learning directly from a good friend of his father named Marco Aurélio. Over time, Bittencourt’s training was passed on to a few different instructors, namely Gabriel Wilcox (who promoted Breno to yellow belt) and Marco Túlio in Floripa (blue belt) before settling at", "url": ""}, {"name": "Carlson Gracie team", "url": "https://www.bjjheroes.com/featured/carlson-gracie-academy"}, {"name": "in Rio de Janeiro, with", "url": ""}, {"name": "While progressing through the belt system, Breno decided to take a 4 year hiatus to focus on his university degree in Information Technology. Once Bittencourt finished his degree, and found a job in the IT industry he went straight back into jiu jitsu’s competitive scene.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Even though he was equipped with his incredible talent, Breno struggled to break through in jiu jitsu. He soon acknowledged that the sport was no place for the part time grappler, and decided to meet the standard. He quit his full time job to work as a freelancer, so he could dedicate himself to being an athlete.", "url": ""}, {"name": "His hard work started bearing fruits in 2015, as Breno conquered numerous important titles. His hard work paid off with coach Alan Moraes promoting him to black belt on July 2016.", "url": ""}, {"name": "Breno Bittencourt Grappling Record", "url": ""}, {"name": "37 WINS", "url": ""}, {"name": "BY POINTS", "url": ""}, {"name": "BY ADVANTAGES", "url": ""}, {"name": "BY SUBMISSION", "url": ""}, {"name": "BY DECISION", "url": ""}, {"name": "BY PENALTIES", "url": ""}, {"name": "BY DQ", "url": ""}, {"name": "8 SUBMISSIONS WINS", "url": ""}, {"name": "#214eb8", "url": ""}, {"name": "Choke from back", "url": ""}, {"name": "#86e620", "url": ""}, {"name": "RNC", "url": ""}, {"name": "#5AD3D1", "url": ""}, {"name": "Triangle", "url": ""}, {"name": "#d1212a", "url": ""}, {"name": "No arm triangle", "url": ""}, {"name": "#fad11b", "url": ""}, {"name": "Botinha", "url": ""}, {"name": "(100%)", "url": ""}, {"name": "SUBMISSIONS", "url": ""}, {"name": "<div class="progress"", "url": ""}, {"name": "</div", "url": ""}, {"name": "25 LOSSES", "url": ""}, {"name": "9 SUBMISSIONS LOSSES", "url": ""}, {"name": "Kimura", "url": ""}, {"name": "Armbar", "url": ""}, {"name": "Kneebar", "url": ""}, {"name": "Toe hold", "url": ""}, {"name": "#f58822", "url": ""}, {"name": "Darce choke", "url": ""}, {"name": "#224aba", "url": ""}, {"name": "Breno Bittencourt Fight History", "url": ""}, {"name": "Opp